{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1438605-dumb-hearthstone-question","id":1438605,"title":"Dumb Hearthstone question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-08T13:01:12-08:00","id":1438605,"title":"Dumb Hearthstone question","content":"Do hearthstones have to be socketed in something or could you walk around with it in your hand and get the same effect? Obviously, it wouldn't be as safe or convenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T13:11:28-08:00","id":1438608,"title":"","content":"Depends on the hearthstone. Any hearthstone that says it has to be socketed in an attuned artifact to give a particular benefit, well, has to be socketed in an attuned artifact to give that benefit. The same applies to the count-as-in-the-manse benefit, that requires the hearthstone be socketed in an attuned artifact. <br /> But many hearthstones have a utility feature that does just work even if in your hand or pocket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T13:52:10-08:00","id":1438616,"title":"","content":"Can Hearthstone Amulet (Tiara, Bracer, etc.) hold more than one hearthstone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T14:04:34-08:00","id":1438619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fredo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1438605-dumb-hearthstone-question?p=1438616#post1438616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Hearthstone Amulet (Tiara, Bracer, etc.) hold more than one hearthstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>The writeup in the core book uses strictly singular language (&quot;a socket&quot;, &quot;an attuned hearthstone&quot;). I'd interpret that to mean that you only get one socket per, so need another amulet for each additional socket.<br /> But I also think it'd be entirely reasonable to get a three-dot version with a bunch more sockets, and some fringe benefits or evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","user":"vwllss trnt prncss","date":". 03-08-2021, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T14:05:04-08:00","id":1438620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fredo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1438605-dumb-hearthstone-question?p=1438616#post1438616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Hearthstone Amulet (Tiara, Bracer, etc.) hold more than one hearthstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing generally not, as the text suggests they're single-slotted, but allowing two (e.g. with paired bracers) doesn't seem too broke to me -- you could say that's three-dot and it wouldn't be unreasonable, but at that point you could just get Beloved Adorei and have three sockets <i>and</i> a daiklave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-08-2021, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T14:38:20-08:00","id":1438628,"title":"","content":"I would absolutely allow two hearthstone sockets on a two-dot artifact that does nothing else.<br /> <br /> You could look to 2E's Hearthstone Bracers (and Perfected Kata Bracers) if you wanted to make a 3+-dot artifact with Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-09-2021, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T15:11:05-08:00","id":1438634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1438605-dumb-hearthstone-question?p=1438628#post1438628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could look to 2E's Hearthstone Bracers (and Perfected Kata Bracers) if you wanted to make a 3-dot artifact with Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you remember which book those are in?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T09:33:26-08:00","id":1438755,"title":"","content":"Frankly I think amulets and bracers should do something to warrant costing 2 dots anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T09:58:21-08:00","id":1438759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fredo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1438605-dumb-hearthstone-question?p=1438634#post1438634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you remember which book those are in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hearthstone Bracers are in the 2E Core. They make your attacks better.<br /> Perfected Kata Bracers are in Oadenol's Codex. They make your Martial Arts attacks much better.<br /> <br /> It'd take some work to translate either to the 3E paradigm, but as a starting point (literally just off the top of my head -- this is a concept idea, not a finished idea) you could have something like...<br /> <br /> Perfected Bracers - 3 Dot Artifact<br /> <br /> Attunement: 5m<br /> Hearthstone slots: 2<br /> <br /> Whilst in a Martial Arts Form, your form weapon attacks (but not unarmed martial arts attacks) use the traits of an Artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> Evocation 1 - The bracers are Exceptional Equipment for Feats of Demolition or teaching Martial Arts you have mastered (know to Form Charm)<br /> Evocation 2 - The bracers upgrade your unarmed martial arts attacks to the artifact statline so long as you are only using the martial art of the Form you are in<br /> Evocation 3 - Gain 1WP when you enter a MA Form reflexively<br /> Evocation 4 - Reflexively Draw/Ready a MA weapon when you enter its Form<br /> Evocation 5 - The bracers upgrade all your unarmed martial arts attacks to the artifact statline so long as you are in any MA Form","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-09-2021, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T19:18:42-08:00","id":1438868,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}